think I REPAIRED THE WRONG LOOP FIRST, and the measurement caught it inside one run. root_finder spawned 515 tr. I read the sites, found three identical subexpressions on consecutive lines, cured them, and the count fell 515 to 479 -- thirty-six removed. That loop runs per SENTINEL, twelve iterations. The 479 lived two hundred lines away in the loop that runs per FINDER, 234 of them, where the same derivation was spelled twice more.
think THE LESSON IS EXACT AND IT IS NOT ABOUT THIS FILE: a site is not a count until its loop is measured. I had the trace all along and read it as a list of sites rather than as sites times iterations. Both spellings look identical in a diff; only the enclosing loop decides which one matters.
obs FIVE PREDICTIONS WERE WRITTEN IN THE CLAIM AND THREE HELD. Byte-identical held, proven against a held-still tree. tr to zero held, 515 to 0. Wall at least halved held, 4,109ms to 1,814ms at 2.3x. Awk below 20 MISSED at 248 of a predicted under-20, and total processes below 150 MISSED at 382.
obs THE MISS TAUGHT THE CLASS ITS BOUNDARY, which is worth more than the prediction would have been. The 248 remaining awk are ONE call at line 183, once per candidate file, and it reads a whole file and scans it across lines. That awk EARNS its process -- shell would be slower rather than faster. So the idiom this seat has now cured four times, a tool spawned for what the shell already does, stops exactly where the tool starts doing tool work.
obs parents_of lost its per-call awk to a map read once and walked in the shell, IFS saved and restored around the walk. That removed roughly seventeen, which is honest and small: its nested loop is narrower than it reads.
